    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30629" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">necrŏmantīa</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-ēa</span></b> ), ae,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεκρομαντεια</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an evoking of
				the dead</i> to reveal the future, <i>necromancy</i>, <i><span class="en">Lact. 2, 16 <i>init.</i></span></i>, Aug. Civ. Dei, 7,
			35.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Necromantea Homeri, <i>that part of the Odyssey in
				which Ulysses descends into the infernal regions</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 35,
				11, 40, § 132</span></i>.</div>
